# Local virtualenvs and tool caches. `uv sync --frozen` recreates .venv from uv.lock, which is
# committed; nothing in here is an input to the build.
#
# .uv-bootstrap is the second virtualenv, and it exists for a reason worth writing down:
# `uv sync --frozen` makes .venv match uv.lock exactly, and uv is not in uv.lock, so installing
# uv into .venv and then running `uv sync` deletes uv. uv lives outside the environment it
# manages. See the "Set-up" section of README.md.
.venv/
.uv-bootstrap/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Written by the CI differential step and by a local harness run; the committed corpus is the
# small smoke one under tests/fixtures/.
differential.jsonl
